fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
# /effort (fx 04a5e3af): the bare menu, its keys, Enter and Escape, an edit
# closing it, the announcement; /effort <level> applied, unavailable,
# malformed, default; a change mid-turn; and which request carried which
# reasoning. The settings file after each change.
#
# The `/effort ` column (Space and Tab after `/effort`, E6) is P5-EF2's and
# is not driven here; nor is `/effort HIGH`, which fx applies through that
# column's Enter (`app_input_runtime.zig:1421@481104fd` ->
# `submitEffortPicker`, whose filter ignores case,
# `input_completion_runtime.zig:1476`), not through the command. `/effort
# low` takes the column's place, so the slow turn runs on `low` as in the
# research run. `slash-ef` also finds fx's `/fork` (its "before"), which is
# P5-FK2's row; `slash-eff` finds `/effort` alone.
models p5-effort-fork-models.json
gateway p5-effort-fork-slow-turns.json
seed p5-effort-fork-seed-astra.json
nomodel
wait 3
snap launch
type /ef
wait 0.6
snap slash-ef
key C-u
wait 0.3
type /eff
wait 0.6
snap slash-eff
key C-u
wait 0.3
type /effort
wait 0.3
key Enter
wait 1
snap menu
key Down
wait 0.3
snap menu-down
key Up Up
wait 0.3
snap menu-wrap
key Escape
wait 0.5
snap menu-esc
type /effort
key Enter
wait 1
key Down Down
wait 0.3
key Enter
wait 1
snap menu-enter
home after-menu-enter
type /effort
key Enter
wait 1
type x
wait 0.4
snap menu-edit
key C-u
wait 0.3
paste /effort high
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-high
home after-high
paste /effort bogus
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-bogus
paste /effort max
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-max
paste /effort two words
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-malformed
paste /effort default
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-default
home after-default
paste /effort low
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-low
home after-low
type slow turn please
key Enter
held
paste /effort high
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap midturn
home after-midturn
release
wait 8
snap midturn-done
type after the change
key Enter
wait 3
snap after-turn
home end
gwlog
